<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Theoretical Results and Proofs</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Proof of Theoretical results in Section <a href="#S3" title="3 Fundamental Limits of LLM Alignment. ‣ Theoretical Limits of Language Model Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> </h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">See <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (Information-Theoretic Limits of Alignment). ‣ 3.1 Information-Theoretic Limits of Alignment ‣ 3 Fundamental Limits of LLM Alignment. ‣ Theoretical Limits of Language Model Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">As per <a href="#S2.E2" title="In 2 Background ‣ Theoretical Limits of Language Model Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a>, the following relationship holds between aligned and base models:</span></p>
<table id="A2.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\pi(r,\lambda)(\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x})}{\pi_{\texttt{base}}(\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x})}=\frac{e^{r(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})/\lambda}}{Z_{r,\lambda}(\mathbf{x})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\pi(r,\lambda)(\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x})}{\pi_{\texttt{base}}(\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x})}=\frac{e^{r(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})/\lambda}}{Z_{r,\lambda}(\mathbf{x})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Taking logarithms both sides gives</span></p>
<table id="A2.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}&amp;\log\pi(r,\lambda)(\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x})-\log\pi_{\texttt{base}}(\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x})=\frac{r(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})}{\lambda}-\log Z_{r,\lambda}(\mathbf{x})\\
\Longrightarrow\quad&amp;r(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})=\lambda\left(\log\frac{\pi(r,\lambda)(\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x})}{\pi_{\texttt{base}}(\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x})}+\log Z_{r,\lambda}(\mathbf{x})\right).\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}&amp;\log\pi(r,\lambda)(\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x})-\log\pi_{\texttt{base}}(\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x})=\frac{r(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})}{\lambda}-\log Z_{r,\lambda}(\mathbf{x})\\
\Longrightarrow\quad&amp;r(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})=\lambda\left(\log\frac{\pi(r,\lambda)(\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x})}{\pi_{\texttt{base}}(\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x})}+\log Z_{r,\lambda}(\mathbf{x})\right).\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Taking the expectation of <a href="#A2.E2" title="In Proof. ‣ B.1 Proof of Theoretical results in Section ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Results and Proofs ‣ Theoretical Limits of Language Model Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a> under <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(r,\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(r,\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> gives</span></p>
<table id="A2.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{y}\sim\pi(r,\lambda)}[r(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})]=\lambda\texttt{KL}\left(\pi(r,\lambda)||\pi_{\texttt{base}}\right)+\lambda\log Z_{r,\lambda}(\mathbf{x})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>λ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">KL</mtext><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{y}\sim\pi(r,\lambda)}[r(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})]=\lambda\texttt{KL}\left(\pi(r,\lambda)||\pi_{\texttt{base}}\right)+\lambda\log Z_{r,\lambda}(\mathbf{x}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">while taking the expectation of <a href="#A2.E2" title="In Proof. ‣ B.1 Proof of Theoretical results in Section ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Results and Proofs ‣ Theoretical Limits of Language Model Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a> under <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\texttt{base}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\texttt{base}}</annotation></semantics></math> similarly yields</span></p>
<table id="A2.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{y}\sim\pi_{\text{base}}}[r(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})]=-\,\lambda\texttt{KL}\big(\pi_{\texttt{base}}||\pi(r,\lambda)\big)+\lambda\log Z_{r,\lambda}(\mathbf{x})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>base</mtext></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.392em">−</mo><mi>λ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">KL</mtext><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{y}\sim\pi_{\text{base}}}[r(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})]=-\,\lambda\texttt{KL}\big(\pi_{\texttt{base}}||\pi(r,\lambda)\big)+\lambda\log Z_{r,\lambda}(\mathbf{x}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.5.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, subtracting the two expectations we get</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{y}\sim\pi(r,\lambda)}[r(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})]-\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{y}\sim\pi_{\texttt{base}}}[r(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})]&amp;=\lambda\left(\texttt{KL}(\pi(r,\lambda)||\pi_{\texttt{base}})+\texttt{KL}(\pi_{\texttt{base}}||\pi(r,\lambda))\right)\\
&amp;={\lambda}\texttt{JD}(\pi(r,\lambda)||\pi_{\texttt{base}}),\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">KL</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">KL</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>λ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">JD</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{y}\sim\pi(r,\lambda)}[r(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})]-\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{y}\sim\pi_{\texttt{base}}}[r(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})]&amp;=\lambda\left(\texttt{KL}(\pi(r,\lambda)||\pi_{\texttt{base}})+\texttt{KL}(\pi_{\texttt{base}}||\pi(r,\lambda))\right)\\
&amp;={\lambda}\texttt{JD}(\pi(r,\lambda)||\pi_{\texttt{base}}),\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.6.1" class="ltx_text">with <span id="A2.SS1.p2.6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">JD</span> denoting Jeffreys divergence, which completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">See <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (Computable Limit of Alignment). ‣ 3.1 Information-Theoretic Limits of Alignment ‣ 3 Fundamental Limits of LLM Alignment. ‣ Theoretical Limits of Language Model Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">First, note that using <a href="#S2.E2" title="In 2 Background ‣ Theoretical Limits of Language Model Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a> we can write the expectation under the aligned model as</span></p>
<table id="A2.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{y}\sim\pi_{r,\lambda}}\left[r^{\prime}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\right]=\sum_{\mathbf{y}\in\mathcal{V}}\frac{\pi_{\texttt{base}}(\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x})e^{r(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})/\lambda}}{\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{y}\sim\pi_{\texttt{base}}}\left[e^{r(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})/\lambda}\right]}\,r^{\prime}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})=\frac{\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{y}\sim\pi_{\texttt{base}}}\left[e^{r(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})/\lambda}\,r^{\prime}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\right]}{\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{y}\sim\pi_{\texttt{base}}}\left[e^{r(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})/\lambda}\right]}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{y}\sim\pi_{r,\lambda}}\left[r^{\prime}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\right]=\sum_{\mathbf{y}\in\mathcal{V}}\frac{\pi_{\texttt{base}}(\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x})e^{r(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})/\lambda}}{\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{y}\sim\pi_{\texttt{base}}}\left[e^{r(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})/\lambda}\right]}\,r^{\prime}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})=\frac{\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{y}\sim\pi_{\texttt{base}}}\left[e^{r(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})/\lambda}\,r^{\prime}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\right]}{\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{y}\sim\pi_{\texttt{base}}}\left[e^{r(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})/\lambda}\right]}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Plugging this into <a href="#S3.E4" title="In Theorem 2 (Computable Limit of Alignment). ‣ 3.1 Information-Theoretic Limits of Alignment ‣ 3 Fundamental Limits of LLM Alignment. ‣ Theoretical Limits of Language Model Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}&amp;\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{y}\sim\pi_{r,\lambda}}\left[r^{\prime}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\right]-\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{y}\sim\pi_{\texttt{base}}}\left[r^{\prime}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\right]\\
=&amp;\frac{\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{y}\sim\pi_{\texttt{base}}}\left[e^{r(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})/\lambda}\,r^{\prime}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\right]}{\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{y}\sim\pi_{\texttt{base}}}\left[e^{r(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})/\lambda}\right]}-\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{y}\sim\pi_{\texttt{base}}}\left[r^{\prime}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\right]\\
=&amp;\frac{\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{y}\sim\pi_{\texttt{base}}}\left[e^{r(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})/\lambda}\,r^{\prime}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\right]-\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{y}\sim\pi_{\texttt{base}}}\left[e^{r(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})/\lambda}\right]\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{y}\sim\pi_{\texttt{base}}}\left[r^{\prime}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\right]}{\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{y}\sim\pi_{\texttt{base}}}\left[e^{r(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})/\lambda}\right]}\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}&amp;\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{y}\sim\pi_{r,\lambda}}\left[r^{\prime}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\right]-\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{y}\sim\pi_{\texttt{base}}}\left[r^{\prime}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\right]\\
=&amp;\frac{\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{y}\sim\pi_{\texttt{base}}}\left[e^{r(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})/\lambda}\,r^{\prime}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\right]}{\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{y}\sim\pi_{\texttt{base}}}\left[e^{r(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})/\lambda}\right]}-\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{y}\sim\pi_{\texttt{base}}}\left[r^{\prime}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\right]\\
=&amp;\frac{\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{y}\sim\pi_{\texttt{base}}}\left[e^{r(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})/\lambda}\,r^{\prime}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\right]-\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{y}\sim\pi_{\texttt{base}}}\left[e^{r(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})/\lambda}\right]\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{y}\sim\pi_{\texttt{base}}}\left[r^{\prime}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\right]}{\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{y}\sim\pi_{\texttt{base}}}\left[e^{r(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})/\lambda}\right]}\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">Note that the numerator in <a href="#A2.E6" title="In Proof. ‣ B.1 Proof of Theoretical results in Section ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Results and Proofs ‣ Theoretical Limits of Language Model Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.6</span></a> is in the form <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[XY]-\mathbb{E}[X]\mathbb{E}[Y]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[XY]-\mathbb{E}[X]\mathbb{E}[Y]</annotation></semantics></math>, which is exactly the covariance between <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math>. This allows us to rewrite <a href="#A2.E6" title="In Proof. ‣ B.1 Proof of Theoretical results in Section ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Results and Proofs ‣ Theoretical Limits of Language Model Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.6</span></a> as</span></p>
<table id="A2.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{y}\sim\pi_{r,\lambda}}\left[r^{\prime}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\right]-\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{y}\sim\pi_{\texttt{base}}}\left[r^{\prime}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\right]&amp;=\frac{\texttt{Cov}_{\pi_{\texttt{base}}}\left(r^{\prime}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}),e^{r(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})/\lambda}\right)}{\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{y}\sim\pi_{\texttt{base}}}\left[e^{r(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})/\lambda}\right]}\\
&amp;=\texttt{Cov}_{\pi_{\texttt{base}}}\left(r^{\prime}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}),\frac{e^{r(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})/\lambda}}{\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{y}\sim\pi_{\texttt{base}}}\left[e^{r(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})/\lambda}\right]}\right),\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Cov</mtext><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Cov</mtext><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{y}\sim\pi_{r,\lambda}}\left[r^{\prime}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\right]-\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{y}\sim\pi_{\texttt{base}}}\left[r^{\prime}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\right]&amp;=\frac{\texttt{Cov}_{\pi_{\texttt{base}}}\left(r^{\prime}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}),e^{r(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})/\lambda}\right)}{\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{y}\sim\pi_{\texttt{base}}}\left[e^{r(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})/\lambda}\right]}\\
&amp;=\texttt{Cov}_{\pi_{\texttt{base}}}\left(r^{\prime}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}),\frac{e^{r(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})/\lambda}}{\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{y}\sim\pi_{\texttt{base}}}\left[e^{r(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})/\lambda}\right]}\right),\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">thus concluding the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">See <a href="#Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 1 (Convergence of Estimator). ‣ 3.2 Estimating the Limits of Alignment from Data ‣ 3 Fundamental Limits of LLM Alignment. ‣ Theoretical Limits of Language Model Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">The proof relies on the Weak Law of Large Numbers (WLLN) and the Continuous Mapping Theorem.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1. Convergence of Component Estimators (WLLN):<span id="A2.SS1.p7.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">The WLLN states that for a sequence of i.i.d. random variables <math id="A2.SS1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{1},\dots,X_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{1},\dots,X_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> with a finite expectation <math id="A2.SS1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[X]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[X]</annotation></semantics></math>, the sample mean <math id="A2.SS1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{X}_{n}=\frac{1}{n}\sum X_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>∑</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{X}_{n}=\frac{1}{n}\sum X_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> converges in probability to the expectation: <math id="A2.SS1.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{X}_{n}\xrightarrow{p}\mathbb{E}[X]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝑝</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{X}_{n}\xrightarrow{p}\mathbb{E}[X]</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">We apply this to our three primary estimators (from Definition <a href="#Thmdefinition1" title="Definition 1 (Monte Carlo Estimator for Δ(𝑟,𝑟^′)). ‣ 3.2 Estimating the Limits of Alignment from Data ‣ 3 Fundamental Limits of LLM Alignment. ‣ Theoretical Limits of Language Model Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>), which are all sample means of i.i.d. variables (since each <math id="A2.SS1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>y</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{(i)}</annotation></semantics></math> is drawn i.i.d. from <math id="A2.SS1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\text{base}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>base</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\text{base}}</annotation></semantics></math>):</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ul id="A2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mu}_{r^{\prime}}\xrightarrow{p}\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\text{base}}}[r^{\prime}(y)]=\mu_{r^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝑝</mo></mover><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>base</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mu}_{r^{\prime}}\xrightarrow{p}\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\text{base}}}[r^{\prime}(y)]=\mu_{r^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{Z}_{r}\xrightarrow{p}\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\text{base}}}[\exp(r(y)/\lambda)]=Z_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>r</mi></msub><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝑝</mo></mover><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>base</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{Z}_{r}\xrightarrow{p}\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\text{base}}}[\exp(r(y)/\lambda)]=Z_{r}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{C}\xrightarrow{p}\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\text{base}}}[r^{\prime}(y)\cdot\exp(r(y)/\lambda)]=C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝑝</mo></mover><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>base</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{C}\xrightarrow{p}\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\text{base}}}[r^{\prime}(y)\cdot\exp(r(y)/\lambda)]=C</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A2.SS1.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">This holds because we assumed these expectations are finite.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">2. Convergence of Combined Estimators (Continuous Mapping):<span id="A2.SS1.p11.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">The Continuous Mapping Theorem states that for a sequence of random variables <math id="A2.SS1.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{n}\xrightarrow{p}c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝑝</mo></mover><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{n}\xrightarrow{p}c</annotation></semantics></math>, and a function <math id="A2.SS1.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> that is continuous at <math id="A2.SS1.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A2.SS1.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(X_{n})\xrightarrow{p}g(c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝑝</mo></mover><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(X_{n})\xrightarrow{p}g(c)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p13" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">The covariance estimator <math id="A2.SS1.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\text{Cov}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mtext>Cov</mtext><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\text{Cov}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a continuous function <math id="A2.SS1.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> of our three sample means:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\text{Cov}}=g_{1}(\hat{C},\hat{\mu}_{r^{\prime}},\hat{Z}_{r})=\hat{C}-(\hat{\mu}_{r^{\prime}}\cdot\hat{Z}_{r})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mtext>Cov</mtext><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\text{Cov}}=g_{1}(\hat{C},\hat{\mu}_{r^{\prime}},\hat{Z}_{r})=\hat{C}-(\hat{\mu}_{r^{\prime}}\cdot\hat{Z}_{r})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p13.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p13.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since multiplication and subtraction are continuous functions, and all arguments converge in probability to their respective limits, the estimator <math id="A2.SS1.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\text{Cov}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mtext>Cov</mtext><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\text{Cov}}</annotation></semantics></math> converges in probability to the true covariance:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\text{Cov}}\xrightarrow{p}C-\mu_{r^{\prime}}Z_{r}=\text{Cov}_{\pi_{\text{base}}}(r^{\prime},\exp(r/\lambda))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mtext>Cov</mtext><mo>^</mo></mover><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝑝</mo></mover><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mtext>Cov</mtext><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>base</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\text{Cov}}\xrightarrow{p}C-\mu_{r^{\prime}}Z_{r}=\text{Cov}_{\pi_{\text{base}}}(r^{\prime},\exp(r/\lambda))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p14" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, the gain estimator <math id="A2.SS1.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\Delta}_{n}(r,r^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\Delta}_{n}(r,r^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> is a continuous function <math id="A2.SS1.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A2.SS1.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\text{Cov}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mtext>Cov</mtext><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\text{Cov}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.p14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{Z}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{Z}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\Delta}_{n}(r,r^{\prime})=g_{2}(\widehat{\text{Cov}},\hat{Z}_{r})=\frac{\widehat{\text{Cov}}}{\hat{Z}_{r}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mtext>Cov</mtext><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mover accent="true"><mtext>Cov</mtext><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>r</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\Delta}_{n}(r,r^{\prime})=g_{2}(\widehat{\text{Cov}},\hat{Z}_{r})=\frac{\widehat{\text{Cov}}}{\hat{Z}_{r}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p14.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p14.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since division is a continuous function (given our assumption that the denominator <math id="A2.SS1.p14.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{r}\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{r}\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>), <math id="A2.SS1.p14.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\Delta}_{n}(r,r^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\Delta}_{n}(r,r^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> converges in probability to the true gain <math id="A2.SS1.p14.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(r,r^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(r,r^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\Delta}_{n}(r,r^{\prime})\xrightarrow{p}\frac{\text{Cov}_{\pi_{\text{base}}}(r^{\prime},\exp(r/\lambda))}{Z_{r}}=\Delta(r,r^{\prime})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝑝</mo></mover><mfrac><mrow><msub><mtext>Cov</mtext><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>base</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\Delta}_{n}(r,r^{\prime})\xrightarrow{p}\frac{\text{Cov}_{\pi_{\text{base}}}(r^{\prime},\exp(r/\lambda))}{Z_{r}}=\Delta(r,r^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p14.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p14.3.1" class="ltx_text">Showing that <math id="A2.SS1.p14.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\Delta}_{n}(r,r^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\Delta}_{n}(r,r^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> converges to <math id="A2.SS1.p14.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(r,r^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(r,r^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p15.1" class="ltx_p">See <a href="#Thmproposition2" title="Proposition 2 (Convergence of KL Estimators). ‣ 3.2 Estimating the Limits of Alignment from Data ‣ 3 Fundamental Limits of LLM Alignment. ‣ Theoretical Limits of Language Model Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS1.p16" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text">Taking logarithms in equation <a href="#S2.E2" title="In 2 Background ‣ Theoretical Limits of Language Model Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a> gives <math id="A2.SS1.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\frac{\pi_{r,\lambda}(\mathbf{y}|\mathbf{x})}{\pi_{\texttt{base}}(\mathbf{y}|\mathbf{x})}=r(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})/\lambda-\log Z(\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\frac{\pi_{r,\lambda}(\mathbf{y}|\mathbf{x})}{\pi_{\texttt{base}}(\mathbf{y}|\mathbf{x})}=r(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})/\lambda-\log Z(\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math>, so taking expectation under <math id="A2.SS1.p16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{r,\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{r,\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> yields the population quantity</span></p>
<table id="A2.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E8.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\texttt{KL}(\pi_{r,\lambda}\|\pi_{\texttt{base}})=\frac{\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{r,\lambda}}[r]}{\lambda}-\log Z=\frac{\mu_{r}+\Delta(r,r)}{\lambda}-\log Z," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">KL</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{KL}(\pi_{r,\lambda}\|\pi_{\texttt{base}})=\frac{\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{r,\lambda}}[r]}{\lambda}-\log Z=\frac{\mu_{r}+\Delta(r,r)}{\lambda}-\log Z,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p16.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p16.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the second equality uses <math id="A2.SS1.p16.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{r,\lambda}}[r]=\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\texttt{base}}}[r]+\Delta(r,r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{r,\lambda}}[r]=\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\texttt{base}}}[r]+\Delta(r,r)</annotation></semantics></math> from <a href="#S3.E4" title="In Theorem 2 (Computable Limit of Alignment). ‣ 3.1 Information-Theoretic Limits of Alignment ‣ 3 Fundamental Limits of LLM Alignment. ‣ Theoretical Limits of Language Model Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a>.
The estimator <math id="A2.SS1.p16.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widehat{\texttt{KL}}(\pi_{r,\lambda}\|\pi_{\texttt{base}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">KL</mtext><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\texttt{KL}}(\pi_{r,\lambda}\|\pi_{\texttt{base}})</annotation></semantics></math> replaces each population quantity with its sample counterpart:</span></p>
<ol id="A2.I2" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mu}_{r}\xrightarrow{p}\mu_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>r</mi></msub><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝑝</mo></mover><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mu}_{r}\xrightarrow{p}\mu_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> by the WLLN.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\Delta}_{n}(r,r)\xrightarrow{p}\Delta(r,r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝑝</mo></mover><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\Delta}_{n}(r,r)\xrightarrow{p}\Delta(r,r)</annotation></semantics></math> by <a href="#Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 1 (Convergence of Estimator). ‣ 3.2 Estimating the Limits of Alignment from Data ‣ 3 Fundamental Limits of LLM Alignment. ‣ Theoretical Limits of Language Model Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Prop.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, finiteness conditions are satisfied by hypothesis.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{Z}_{r}\xrightarrow{p}Z_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>r</mi></msub><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝑝</mo></mover><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{Z}_{r}\xrightarrow{p}Z_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> by the WLLN, since <math id="A2.I2.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\exp(r/\lambda)]=Z_{r}&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\exp(r/\lambda)]=Z_{r}&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math> by hypothesis; then <math id="A2.I2.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\widehat{Z}_{r}\xrightarrow{p}\log Z_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝑝</mo></mover><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\widehat{Z}_{r}\xrightarrow{p}\log Z_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> by the Continuous Mapping Theorem, since <math id="A2.I2.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{r}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{r}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A2.SS1.p16.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p16.3.1" class="ltx_text">The estimator is a continuous function of these three convergent quantities, so by a further application of the Continuous Mapping Theorem, <math id="A2.SS1.p16.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widehat{\texttt{KL}}(\pi_{r,\lambda}\|\pi_{\texttt{base}})\xrightarrow{p}\texttt{KL}(\pi_{r,\lambda}\|\pi_{\texttt{base}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">KL</mtext><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝑝</mo></mover><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">KL</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\texttt{KL}}(\pi_{r,\lambda}\|\pi_{\texttt{base}})\xrightarrow{p}\texttt{KL}(\pi_{r,\lambda}\|\pi_{\texttt{base}})</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Proof of Theoretical results in Section <a href="#S4" title="4 Proxy Rewards and a Justification for Reward Ensembling ‣ Theoretical Limits of Language Model Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a></h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">See <a href="#Thmproposition3" title="Proposition 3 (The Impact of Proxy Rewards). ‣ 4.1 The Impact of Proxy Rewards in Reward Hacking ‣ 4 Proxy Rewards and a Justification for Reward Ensembling ‣ Theoretical Limits of Language Model Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fix a query <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math> and work conditionally on <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Define the two partition functions</span></p>
<table id="A2.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{\ast}\triangleq\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{y}\sim\pi_{\texttt{base}}}\big[e^{r^{*}(\mathbf{y})/\lambda}\big],\qquad Z_{\sim}\triangleq\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{y}\sim\pi_{\texttt{base}}}\big[e^{\tilde{r}(\mathbf{y})/\lambda}\big]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>≜</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mo>∼</mo></msub><mo>≜</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{\ast}\triangleq\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{y}\sim\pi_{\texttt{base}}}\big[e^{r^{*}(\mathbf{y})/\lambda}\big],\qquad Z_{\sim}\triangleq\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{y}\sim\pi_{\texttt{base}}}\big[e^{\tilde{r}(\mathbf{y})/\lambda}\big],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">and recall that <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{y})=\tilde{r}(\mathbf{y})-r^{*}(\mathbf{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{y})=\tilde{r}(\mathbf{y})-r^{*}(\mathbf{y})</annotation></semantics></math> is the preference residual.
Applying <a href="#S3.E4" title="In Theorem 2 (Computable Limit of Alignment). ‣ 3.1 Information-Theoretic Limits of Alignment ‣ 3 Fundamental Limits of LLM Alignment. ‣ Theoretical Limits of Language Model Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.4</span></a> with alignment reward <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=r^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=r^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and evaluation reward <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{\prime}=r^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{\prime}=r^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, and again with <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=\tilde{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=\tilde{r}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{\prime}=r^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{\prime}=r^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, gives</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{r^{*},\lambda}}[r^{*}]-\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\texttt{base}}}[r^{*}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{r^{*},\lambda}}[r^{*}]-\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\texttt{base}}}[r^{*}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\texttt{Cov}_{\mathbf{y}\sim\pi_{\texttt{base}}}\!\left(r^{*}(\mathbf{y}),\,\tfrac{e^{r^{*}(\mathbf{y})/\lambda}}{Z_{\ast}}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Cov</mtext><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi>Z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\texttt{Cov}_{\mathbf{y}\sim\pi_{\texttt{base}}}\!\left(r^{*}(\mathbf{y}),\,\tfrac{e^{r^{*}(\mathbf{y})/\lambda}}{Z_{\ast}}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\tilde{r},\lambda}}[r^{*}]-\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\texttt{base}}}[r^{*}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\tilde{r},\lambda}}[r^{*}]-\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\texttt{base}}}[r^{*}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\texttt{Cov}_{\mathbf{y}\sim\pi_{\texttt{base}}}\!\left(r^{*}(\mathbf{y}),\,\tfrac{e^{\tilde{r}(\mathbf{y})/\lambda}}{Z_{\sim}}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Cov</mtext><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi>Z</mi><mo>∼</mo></msub></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\texttt{Cov}_{\mathbf{y}\sim\pi_{\texttt{base}}}\!\left(r^{*}(\mathbf{y}),\,\tfrac{e^{\tilde{r}(\mathbf{y})/\lambda}}{Z_{\sim}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Subtracting the second from the first, the <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\texttt{base}}}[r^{*}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\texttt{base}}}[r^{*}]</annotation></semantics></math> terms cancel, and linearity of the covariance in the second argument yields</span></p>
<table id="A2.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{r^{*},\lambda}}[r^{*}]-\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\tilde{r},\lambda}}[r^{*}]=\texttt{Cov}_{\mathbf{y}\sim\pi_{\texttt{base}}}\!\left(r^{*}(\mathbf{y}),\,\frac{e^{r^{*}(\mathbf{y})/\lambda}}{Z_{\ast}}-\frac{e^{\tilde{r}(\mathbf{y})/\lambda}}{Z_{\sim}}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Cov</mtext><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi>Z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi>Z</mi><mo>∼</mo></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{r^{*},\lambda}}[r^{*}]-\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\tilde{r},\lambda}}[r^{*}]=\texttt{Cov}_{\mathbf{y}\sim\pi_{\texttt{base}}}\!\left(r^{*}(\mathbf{y}),\,\frac{e^{r^{*}(\mathbf{y})/\lambda}}{Z_{\ast}}-\frac{e^{\tilde{r}(\mathbf{y})/\lambda}}{Z_{\sim}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">Algebraic factorization of the second argument and the substitution <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}=\tilde{r}-r^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}=\tilde{r}-r^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> give</span></p>
<table id="A2.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{e^{r^{*}/\lambda}}{Z_{\ast}}-\frac{e^{\tilde{r}/\lambda}}{Z_{\sim}}=\frac{e^{r^{*}/\lambda}}{Z_{\ast}}\left(1-\frac{Z_{\ast}}{Z_{\sim}}\,e^{(\tilde{r}-r^{*})/\lambda}\right)=\frac{e^{r^{*}/\lambda}}{Z_{\ast}}\left(1-\frac{Z_{\ast}}{Z_{\sim}}\,e^{\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{y})/\lambda}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi>Z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi>Z</mi><mo>∼</mo></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi>Z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>Z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><msub><mi>Z</mi><mo>∼</mo></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi>Z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>Z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><msub><mi>Z</mi><mo>∼</mo></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{e^{r^{*}/\lambda}}{Z_{\ast}}-\frac{e^{\tilde{r}/\lambda}}{Z_{\sim}}=\frac{e^{r^{*}/\lambda}}{Z_{\ast}}\left(1-\frac{Z_{\ast}}{Z_{\sim}}\,e^{(\tilde{r}-r^{*})/\lambda}\right)=\frac{e^{r^{*}/\lambda}}{Z_{\ast}}\left(1-\frac{Z_{\ast}}{Z_{\sim}}\,e^{\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{y})/\lambda}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p2.5.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting back into equation <a href="#A2.E12" title="In Proof. ‣ B.2 Proof of Theoretical results in Section ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Results and Proofs ‣ Theoretical Limits of Language Model Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.12</span></a> yields</span></p>
<table id="A2.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{r^{*},\lambda}}[r^{*}]-\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\tilde{r},\lambda}}[r^{*}]=\texttt{Cov}_{\mathbf{y}\sim\pi_{\texttt{base}}}\!\left(r^{*}(\mathbf{y}),\,\frac{e^{r^{*}(\mathbf{y})/\lambda}}{Z_{\ast}}\left(1-\frac{Z_{\ast}}{Z_{\sim}}\,e^{\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{y})/\lambda}\right)\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Cov</mtext><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi>Z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>Z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><msub><mi>Z</mi><mo>∼</mo></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{r^{*},\lambda}}[r^{*}]-\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\tilde{r},\lambda}}[r^{*}]=\texttt{Cov}_{\mathbf{y}\sim\pi_{\texttt{base}}}\!\left(r^{*}(\mathbf{y}),\,\frac{e^{r^{*}(\mathbf{y})/\lambda}}{Z_{\ast}}\left(1-\frac{Z_{\ast}}{Z_{\sim}}\,e^{\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{y})/\lambda}\right)\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Next, we express <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{\sim}/Z_{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mo>∼</mo></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{\sim}/Z_{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math> under <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{r^{*},\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{r^{*},\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{Z_{\sim}}{Z_{\ast}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>Z</mi><mo>∼</mo></msub><msub><mi>Z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{Z_{\sim}}{Z_{\ast}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\texttt{base}}}\big[e^{(r^{*}+\mathcal{N})/\lambda}\big]}{\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\texttt{base}}}\big[e^{r^{*}/\lambda}\big]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\texttt{base}}}\big[e^{(r^{*}+\mathcal{N})/\lambda}\big]}{\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\texttt{base}}}\big[e^{r^{*}/\lambda}\big]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{Z_{\ast}}\sum_{\mathbf{y}\in\mathcal{V}}\pi_{\texttt{base}}(\mathbf{y})\,e^{r^{*}(\mathbf{y})/\lambda}\,e^{\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{y})/\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>Z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{Z_{\ast}}\sum_{\mathbf{y}\in\mathcal{V}}\pi_{\texttt{base}}(\mathbf{y})\,e^{r^{*}(\mathbf{y})/\lambda}\,e^{\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{y})/\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{y}\sim\pi_{r^{*},\lambda}}\big[e^{\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{y})/\lambda}\big]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{y}\sim\pi_{r^{*},\lambda}}\big[e^{\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{y})/\lambda}\big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Hence</span></p>
<table id="A2.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{Z_{\ast}}{Z_{\sim}}=\frac{1}{\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{y}\sim\pi_{r^{*},\lambda}}\big[e^{\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{y})/\lambda}\big]}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>Z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><msub><mi>Z</mi><mo>∼</mo></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{Z_{\ast}}{Z_{\sim}}=\frac{1}{\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{y}\sim\pi_{r^{*},\lambda}}\big[e^{\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{y})/\lambda}\big]}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting <a href="#A2.E18" title="In Proof. ‣ B.2 Proof of Theoretical results in Section ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Results and Proofs ‣ Theoretical Limits of Language Model Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.18</span></a> into <a href="#A2.E14" title="In Proof. ‣ B.2 Proof of Theoretical results in Section ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Results and Proofs ‣ Theoretical Limits of Language Model Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.14</span></a>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{r^{*},\lambda}}[r^{*}]-\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\tilde{r},\lambda}}[r^{*}]=\texttt{Cov}_{\mathbf{y}\sim\pi_{\texttt{base}}}\!\left(r^{*}(\mathbf{y}),\,\frac{e^{r^{*}(\mathbf{y})/\lambda}}{Z_{\ast}}\left(1-\frac{e^{\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{y})/\lambda}}{\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{y}\sim\pi_{r^{*},\lambda}}\big[e^{\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{y})/\lambda}\big]}\right)\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Cov</mtext><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi>Z</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{r^{*},\lambda}}[r^{*}]-\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\tilde{r},\lambda}}[r^{*}]=\texttt{Cov}_{\mathbf{y}\sim\pi_{\texttt{base}}}\!\left(r^{*}(\mathbf{y}),\,\frac{e^{r^{*}(\mathbf{y})/\lambda}}{Z_{\ast}}\left(1-\frac{e^{\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{y})/\lambda}}{\mathbb{E}_{\mathbf{y}\sim\pi_{r^{*},\lambda}}\big[e^{\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{y})/\lambda}\big]}\right)\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">which completes our proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">See <a href="#Thmproposition4" title="Proposition 4 (A Deterministic Lipschitz Bound). ‣ 4.2 Why Reward Ensembling Mitigates Reward Hacking ‣ 4 Proxy Rewards and a Justification for Reward Ensembling ‣ Theoretical Limits of Language Model Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Fix a query <math id="A2.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math> and work conditionally on <math id="A2.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math>.
By the tilted-form characterization,</span></p>
<table id="A2.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(r,\lambda)(\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x})=\frac{\pi_{\texttt{base}}(\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x})\,e^{r(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})/\lambda}}{\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\texttt{base}}}[e^{r(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})/\lambda}]}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(r,\lambda)(\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x})=\frac{\pi_{\texttt{base}}(\mathbf{y}\mid\mathbf{x})\,e^{r(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})/\lambda}}{\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\texttt{base}}}[e^{r(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})/\lambda}]}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">Define</span></p>
<table id="A2.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{r}\triangleq\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\texttt{base}}}[e^{r/\lambda}],\qquad w_{r}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\triangleq\frac{e^{r(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})/\lambda}}{Z_{r}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>≜</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≜</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{r}\triangleq\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\texttt{base}}}[e^{r/\lambda}],\qquad w_{r}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\triangleq\frac{e^{r(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})/\lambda}}{Z_{r}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">(and similarly <math id="A2.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{s},w_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{s},w_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.SS2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>; dependence on <math id="A2.SS2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math> is implicit).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">The fundamental limit (covariance) identity applied with alignment
reward <math id="A2.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> and evaluation reward <math id="A2.SS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> gives</span></p>
<table id="A2.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(r,r^{*})=\mathbb{E}_{\pi(r,\lambda)}[r^{*}]-\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\texttt{base}}}[r^{*}]=\texttt{Cov}_{\pi_{\texttt{base}}}(r^{*},w_{r})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Cov</mtext><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(r,r^{*})=\mathbb{E}_{\pi(r,\lambda)}[r^{*}]-\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\texttt{base}}}[r^{*}]=\texttt{Cov}_{\pi_{\texttt{base}}}(r^{*},w_{r}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">Similarly,</span></p>
<table id="A2.E23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(s,r^{*})=\texttt{Cov}_{\pi_{\texttt{base}}}(r^{*},w_{s})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Cov</mtext><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(s,r^{*})=\texttt{Cov}_{\pi_{\texttt{base}}}(r^{*},w_{s}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore</span></p>
<table id="A2.E24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(r,r^{*})-\Delta(s,r^{*})=\texttt{Cov}_{\pi_{\texttt{base}}}\big(r^{*},w_{r}-w_{s}\big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Cov</mtext><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(r,r^{*})-\Delta(s,r^{*})=\texttt{Cov}_{\pi_{\texttt{base}}}\big(r^{*},w_{r}-w_{s}\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Cauchy-Schwarz,</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|\Delta(r,r^{*})-\Delta(s,r^{*})|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|\Delta(r,r^{*})-\Delta(s,r^{*})|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E25.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=|\texttt{Cov}_{\pi_{\texttt{base}}}\big(r^{*},w_{r}-w_{s}\big)|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Cov</mtext><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=|\texttt{Cov}_{\pi_{\texttt{base}}}\big(r^{*},w_{r}-w_{s}\big)|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\texttt{Var}(r^{*})^{1/2}\texttt{Var}(w_{r}-w_{s})^{1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\texttt{Var}(r^{*})^{1/2}\texttt{Var}(w_{r}-w_{s})^{1/2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\texttt{Var}(r^{*})^{1/2}\mathbb{E}[(w_{r}-w_{s})^{2}]^{1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\texttt{Var}(r^{*})^{1/2}\mathbb{E}[(w_{r}-w_{s})^{2}]^{1/2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\texttt{Var}(r^{*})^{1/2}\|w_{r}-w_{s}\|_{L^{2}(\pi_{\texttt{base}})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\texttt{Var}(r^{*})^{1/2}\|w_{r}-w_{s}\|_{L^{2}(\pi_{\texttt{base}})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">We now bound <math id="A2.SS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|w_{r}-w_{s}\|_{L^{2}(\pi_{\texttt{base}})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|w_{r}-w_{s}\|_{L^{2}(\pi_{\texttt{base}})}</annotation></semantics></math> in terms of <math id="A2.SS2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|r-s\|_{L^{2}(\pi_{\texttt{base}})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|r-s\|_{L^{2}(\pi_{\texttt{base}})}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Again by Cauchy-Schwarz,</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|\Delta(r,r^{*})-\Delta(s,r^{*})|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|\Delta(r,r^{*})-\Delta(s,r^{*})|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E29.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=|\texttt{Cov}_{\pi_{\texttt{base}}}\big(r^{*},w_{r}-w_{s}\big)|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Cov</mtext><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=|\texttt{Cov}_{\pi_{\texttt{base}}}\big(r^{*},w_{r}-w_{s}\big)|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\texttt{Var}(r^{*})^{1/2}\texttt{Var}(w_{r}-w_{s})^{1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\texttt{Var}(r^{*})^{1/2}\texttt{Var}(w_{r}-w_{s})^{1/2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">We now want to bound the term <math id="A2.SS2.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{r,s}=\texttt{Var}[w_{r}-w_{s}]^{1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{r,s}=\texttt{Var}[w_{r}-w_{s}]^{1/2}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS2.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[(r-s)^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[(r-s)^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math>. Notice that <math id="A2.SS2.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[w_{r}]=\mathbb{E}[w_{s}]=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[w_{r}]=\mathbb{E}[w_{s}]=1</annotation></semantics></math>, as they are both normalized quantities, implying that <math id="A2.SS2.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{Var}[w_{r}-w_{s}]=\mathbb{E}[(w_{r}-w_{s})^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{Var}[w_{r}-w_{s}]=\mathbb{E}[(w_{r}-w_{s})^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math>. We define <math id="A2.SS2.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> as the interpolation</span></p>
<table id="A2.E31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E31.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="w_{t}=\frac{e^{\frac{s+(r-s)t}{\lambda}}}{Z_{t}},\qquad\text{with}\qquad Z_{t}=\mathbb{E}[e^{\frac{s+(r-s)t}{\lambda}]}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>λ</mi></mfrac></msup><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mtext>with</mtext><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{t}=\frac{e^{\frac{s+(r-s)t}{\lambda}}}{Z_{t}},\qquad\text{with}\qquad Z_{t}=\mathbb{E}[e^{\frac{s+(r-s)t}{\lambda}]}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p8.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p8.4.1" class="ltx_text">By the fundamental theorem of calculus, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.E32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{r}-w_{s}=\int_{0}^{1}\left(\frac{d}{dt}w_{t}\right)\,dt=\frac{1}{\lambda}\int_{0}^{1}w_{t}((r-s)-\mathbb{E}[w_{t}(r-s)])\,dt," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{r}-w_{s}=\int_{0}^{1}\left(\frac{d}{dt}w_{t}\right)\,dt=\frac{1}{\lambda}\int_{0}^{1}w_{t}((r-s)-\mathbb{E}[w_{t}(r-s)])\,dt,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p8.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p8.5.1" class="ltx_text">which we can directly substitute inside <math id="A2.SS2.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[(w_{r}-w_{s})^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[(w_{r}-w_{s})^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A2.E33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}V_{r,s}&amp;=\mathbb{E}[(w_{r}-w_{s})^{2}]=\frac{1}{\lambda^{2}}\mathbb{E}\left[\left(\int_{0}^{1}w_{t}((r-s)-\mathbb{E}[w_{t}(r-s)])\,dt\right)^{2}\right]\\
&amp;\leq\frac{1}{\lambda^{2}}\mathbb{E}\left[\int_{0}^{1}w_{t}^{2}\left((r-s)-\mathbb{E}[w_{t}(r-s)]\right)^{2}\,dt\right]\\
&amp;=\frac{1}{\lambda^{2}}\int_{0}^{1}\mathbb{E}\left[w_{t}^{2}\left((r-s)-\mathbb{E}[w_{t}(r-s)]\right)^{2}\right]\,dt\\
&amp;\leq\frac{W}{\lambda^{2}}\int_{0}^{1}\mathbb{E}\left[w_{t}\left((r-s)-\mathbb{E}[w_{t}(r-s)]\right)^{2}\right]\,dt\\
&amp;=\frac{W}{\lambda^{2}}\int_{0}^{1}\texttt{Var}_{w_{t}}\left[r-s\right]\,dt,\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">d</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">d</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>W</mi><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>W</mi><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Var</mtext><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">d</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}V_{r,s}&amp;=\mathbb{E}[(w_{r}-w_{s})^{2}]=\frac{1}{\lambda^{2}}\mathbb{E}\left[\left(\int_{0}^{1}w_{t}((r-s)-\mathbb{E}[w_{t}(r-s)])\,dt\right)^{2}\right]\\
&amp;\leq\frac{1}{\lambda^{2}}\mathbb{E}\left[\int_{0}^{1}w_{t}^{2}\left((r-s)-\mathbb{E}[w_{t}(r-s)]\right)^{2}\,dt\right]\\
&amp;=\frac{1}{\lambda^{2}}\int_{0}^{1}\mathbb{E}\left[w_{t}^{2}\left((r-s)-\mathbb{E}[w_{t}(r-s)]\right)^{2}\right]\,dt\\
&amp;\leq\frac{W}{\lambda^{2}}\int_{0}^{1}\mathbb{E}\left[w_{t}\left((r-s)-\mathbb{E}[w_{t}(r-s)]\right)^{2}\right]\,dt\\
&amp;=\frac{W}{\lambda^{2}}\int_{0}^{1}\texttt{Var}_{w_{t}}\left[r-s\right]\,dt,\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p8.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p8.6.1" class="ltx_text">where we applied Cauchy-Schwarz to swap square and integral, Fubini-Tonelli to swap <math id="A2.SS2.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔼</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.p8.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int_{0}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int_{0}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, and a bound on the tilting function, <math id="A2.SS2.p8.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W=\sup_{t\in[0,1]}\|w_{t}\|_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W=\sup_{t\in[0,1]}\|w_{t}\|_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math>, to extract a <math id="A2.SS2.p8.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> factor from within <math id="A2.SS2.p8.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝔼</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}</annotation></semantics></math>. The constant <math id="A2.SS2.p8.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> admits two complementary bounds depending on the assumption we can make on our reward models. If the rewards are bounded, i.e., <math id="A2.SS2.p8.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|r(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})|,|s(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})|\leq B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|r(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})|,|s(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})|\leq B</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.SS2.p8.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐲</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{y}</annotation></semantics></math>, then also <math id="A2.SS2.p8.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|r_{t}|=|(1-t)s+tr|\leq B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|r_{t}|=|(1-t)s+tr|\leq B</annotation></semantics></math>, giving</span></p>
<table id="A2.E34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{t}(\mathbf{y})=\frac{e^{r_{t}(\mathbf{y})/\lambda}}{Z_{t}}\leq\frac{e^{B/\lambda}}{e^{-B/\lambda}}=e^{2B/\lambda}\eqqcolon W_{B}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mrow><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mo>≕</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{t}(\mathbf{y})=\frac{e^{r_{t}(\mathbf{y})/\lambda}}{Z_{t}}\leq\frac{e^{B/\lambda}}{e^{-B/\lambda}}=e^{2B/\lambda}\eqqcolon W_{B},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p8.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p8.7.1" class="ltx_text">since the numerator is at most <math id="A2.SS2.p8.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{B/\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{B/\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> and the partition function satisfies <math id="A2.SS2.p8.m19" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="Z_{t}=\mathbb{E}[e^{r_{t}/\lambda}]\geq e^{-B/\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{t}=\mathbb{E}[e^{r_{t}/\lambda}]\geq e^{-B/\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math>.
When rewards are unbounded, we can instead exploit the fact that <math id="A2.SS2.p8.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> contains the term <math id="A2.SS2.p8.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\texttt{base}}(\mathbf{y})\,e^{r_{t}(\mathbf{y})/\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\texttt{base}}(\mathbf{y})\,e^{r_{t}(\mathbf{y})/\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math>, so that</span></p>
<table id="A2.E35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{t}(\mathbf{y})=\frac{e^{r_{t}(\mathbf{y})/\lambda}}{Z_{t}}\leq\frac{e^{r_{t}(\mathbf{y})/\lambda}}{\pi_{\texttt{base}}(\mathbf{y})\,e^{r_{t}(\mathbf{y})/\lambda}}=(\pi_{\texttt{base}}(\mathbf{y}))^{-1}\eqqcolon W_{U}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>≕</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>U</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{t}(\mathbf{y})=\frac{e^{r_{t}(\mathbf{y})/\lambda}}{Z_{t}}\leq\frac{e^{r_{t}(\mathbf{y})/\lambda}}{\pi_{\texttt{base}}(\mathbf{y})\,e^{r_{t}(\mathbf{y})/\lambda}}=(\pi_{\texttt{base}}(\mathbf{y}))^{-1}\eqqcolon W_{U},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p8.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p8.8.1" class="ltx_text">which depends only on the base model and is always finite when <math id="A2.SS2.p8.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\texttt{base}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\texttt{base}}</annotation></semantics></math> has finite full support – as is the case for language models with finite vocabulary and bounded generation length. In practice, then, we can write</span></p>
<table id="A2.E36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W=\sup_{t\in[0,1]}\|w_{t}\|_{\infty}\leq\min\left\{W_{B},W_{U}\right\}=\min\left\{e^{2B/\lambda},(\pi_{\texttt{base}}(\mathbf{y}))^{-1}\right\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>U</mi></msub><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W=\sup_{t\in[0,1]}\|w_{t}\|_{\infty}\leq\min\left\{W_{B},W_{U}\right\}=\min\left\{e^{2B/\lambda},(\pi_{\texttt{base}}(\mathbf{y}))^{-1}\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Notice moreover that a property of the exponential family of distributions is that its <math id="A2.SS2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>log</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log</annotation></semantics></math>-partition is the cumulant generating function, and in particular</span></p>
<table id="A2.E37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d^{2}}{dt^{2}}\log Z_{t}=\frac{1}{\lambda}\frac{d}{dt}\mathbb{E}[w_{t}(r-s)]=\frac{1}{\lambda^{2}}\texttt{Var}_{w_{t}}[r-s]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Var</mtext><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d^{2}}{dt^{2}}\log Z_{t}=\frac{1}{\lambda}\frac{d}{dt}\mathbb{E}[w_{t}(r-s)]=\frac{1}{\lambda^{2}}\texttt{Var}_{w_{t}}[r-s],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">which allows us to re-write</span></p>
<table id="A2.E38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{r,s}\leq\frac{W}{\lambda}\int_{0}^{1}\frac{1}{\lambda}\texttt{Var}_{w_{t}}\left[r-s\right]\,dt=\frac{W}{\lambda}\int_{0}^{1}\frac{d}{dt}\mathbb{E}[w_{t}(r-s)]\,dt=\frac{W}{\lambda}\mathbb{E}[(w_{r}-w_{s})(r-s)]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>W</mi><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Var</mtext><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>W</mi><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>W</mi><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{r,s}\leq\frac{W}{\lambda}\int_{0}^{1}\frac{1}{\lambda}\texttt{Var}_{w_{t}}\left[r-s\right]\,dt=\frac{W}{\lambda}\int_{0}^{1}\frac{d}{dt}\mathbb{E}[w_{t}(r-s)]\,dt=\frac{W}{\lambda}\mathbb{E}[(w_{r}-w_{s})(r-s)].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.38)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p9.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p9.3.1" class="ltx_text">Applying Cauchy-Schwarz once again gives</span></p>
<table id="A2.E39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{r,s}=\texttt{Var}[w_{r}-w_{s}]\leq\frac{W}{\lambda}\mathbb{E}[(w_{r}-w_{s})(r-s)]\leq\frac{W}{\lambda}\sqrt{\texttt{Var}[w_{r}-w_{s}]\texttt{Var}[r-s]}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>W</mi><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>W</mi><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{r,s}=\texttt{Var}[w_{r}-w_{s}]\leq\frac{W}{\lambda}\mathbb{E}[(w_{r}-w_{s})(r-s)]\leq\frac{W}{\lambda}\sqrt{\texttt{Var}[w_{r}-w_{s}]\texttt{Var}[r-s]}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.39)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p9.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p9.4.1" class="ltx_text">The variance of <math id="A2.SS2.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r-s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r-s</annotation></semantics></math> can be bound by its second moment. Dividing both sides by <math id="A2.SS2.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{\texttt{Var}[w_{r}-w_{s}]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{\texttt{Var}[w_{r}-w_{s}]}</annotation></semantics></math> provides the bound we are looking for:</span></p>
<table id="A2.E40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{\texttt{Var}[w_{r}-w_{s}]}\leq\frac{W}{\lambda}\sqrt{\mathbb{E}[(r-s)^{2}]}=\frac{W}{\lambda}\|r-s\|_{L^{2}(\pi_{\texttt{base}})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>W</mi><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>W</mi><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{\texttt{Var}[w_{r}-w_{s}]}\leq\frac{W}{\lambda}\sqrt{\mathbb{E}[(r-s)^{2}]}=\frac{W}{\lambda}\|r-s\|_{L^{2}(\pi_{\texttt{base}})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.40)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p9.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p9.5.1" class="ltx_text">Combining with <a href="#A2.E30" title="In Proof. ‣ B.2 Proof of Theoretical results in Section ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Results and Proofs ‣ Theoretical Limits of Language Model Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.30</span></a> completes the proof:</span></p>
<table id="A2.E41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\Delta(r,r^{*})-\Delta(s,r^{*})|\leq\texttt{Var}(r^{*})^{1/2}\texttt{Var}(w_{r}-w_{s})^{1/2}\leq\frac{W}{\lambda}\texttt{Var}(r^{*})^{1/2}\|r-s\|_{L^{2}(\pi_{\texttt{base}})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>W</mi><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\Delta(r,r^{*})-\Delta(s,r^{*})|\leq\texttt{Var}(r^{*})^{1/2}\texttt{Var}(w_{r}-w_{s})^{1/2}\leq\frac{W}{\lambda}\texttt{Var}(r^{*})^{1/2}\|r-s\|_{L^{2}(\pi_{\texttt{base}})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.41)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p11.1" class="ltx_p">See <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3 (Rate of Convergence for Reward Ensemble). ‣ 4.2 Why Reward Ensembling Mitigates Reward Hacking ‣ 4 Proxy Rewards and a Justification for Reward Ensembling ‣ Theoretical Limits of Language Model Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS2.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A2.SS2.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(r)</annotation></semantics></math> denote the post-RLHF true reward when we align with
reward <math id="A2.SS2.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e.,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(r)\;\triangleq\;\mathbb{E}_{\pi(r,\lambda)}[r^{*}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≜</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(r)\;\triangleq\;\mathbb{E}_{\pi(r,\lambda)}[r^{*}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p12.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p12.2.1" class="ltx_text">In particular,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(R_{n})=\mathbb{E}_{\pi(R_{n},\lambda)}[r^{*}],\qquad\Delta(r^{*})=\mathbb{E}_{\pi(r^{*},\lambda)}[r^{*}]=\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{r^{*},\lambda}}[r^{*}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(R_{n})=\mathbb{E}_{\pi(R_{n},\lambda)}[r^{*}],\qquad\Delta(r^{*})=\mathbb{E}_{\pi(r^{*},\lambda)}[r^{*}]=\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{r^{*},\lambda}}[r^{*}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p13" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">By the deterministic Lipschitz bound (proved earlier), there exists a
constant <math id="A2.SS2.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A2.E42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big|\Delta(r)-\Delta(r^{*})\big|\;\leq\;C\times\texttt{Var}(r^{*})^{1/2}\|r-r^{*}\|_{L^{2}(\pi_{\texttt{base}})}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Var</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big|\Delta(r)-\Delta(r^{*})\big|\;\leq\;C\times\texttt{Var}(r^{*})^{1/2}\|r-r^{*}\|_{L^{2}(\pi_{\texttt{base}})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p13.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p13.2.1" class="ltx_text">for all reward functions <math id="A2.SS2.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>, where
<math id="A2.SS2.p13.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|_{L^{2}(\pi_{\texttt{base}})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|_{L^{2}(\pi_{\texttt{base}})}</annotation></semantics></math> is the <math id="A2.SS2.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> norm under the base model <math id="A2.SS2.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\texttt{base}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\texttt{base}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p14" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">Apply equation <a href="#A2.E42" title="In Proof. ‣ B.2 Proof of Theoretical results in Section ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Results and Proofs ‣ Theoretical Limits of Language Model Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.42</span></a> with <math id="A2.SS2.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=R_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=R_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A2.E43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big|\Delta(R_{n})-\Delta(r^{*})\big|\;\leq\;C\times\texttt{Var}(r^{*})^{1/2}\|R_{n}-r^{*}\|_{L^{2}(\pi_{\texttt{base}})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Var</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big|\Delta(R_{n})-\Delta(r^{*})\big|\;\leq\;C\times\texttt{Var}(r^{*})^{1/2}\|R_{n}-r^{*}\|_{L^{2}(\pi_{\texttt{base}})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.43)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p15" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">We now bound the right-hand side in expectation over the randomness of the
ensemble <math id="A2.SS2.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{r_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{r_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Work in the Hilbert space <math id="A2.SS2.p15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}(\pi_{\texttt{base}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}(\pi_{\texttt{base}})</annotation></semantics></math> with inner product
<math id="A2.SS2.p15.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle f,g\rangle=\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\texttt{base}}}[fg]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle f,g\rangle=\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{\texttt{base}}}[fg]</annotation></semantics></math>.
Define the centered random elements</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{i}\;\triangleq\;r_{i}-r^{*},\qquad R_{n}-r^{*}=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\Delta_{i}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≜</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{i}\;\triangleq\;r_{i}-r^{*},\qquad R_{n}-r^{*}=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\Delta_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p16" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text">First compute the second moment of the <math id="A2.SS2.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}(\pi_{\texttt{base}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}(\pi_{\texttt{base}})</annotation></semantics></math>-norm:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\big\|R_{n}-r^{*}\big\|_{L^{2}(\pi_{\texttt{base}})}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\big\|R_{n}-r^{*}\big\|_{L^{2}(\pi_{\texttt{base}})}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\Big\langle\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\Delta_{i},\frac{1}{n}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\Delta_{j}\Big\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\Big\langle\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\Delta_{i},\frac{1}{n}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\Delta_{j}\Big\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n^{2}}\sum_{i,j=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}\langle\Delta_{i},\Delta_{j}\rangle." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n^{2}}\sum_{i,j=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}\langle\Delta_{i},\Delta_{j}\rangle.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.44)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p17" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p17.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p17.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A2.SS2.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{1},\dots,r_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{1},\dots,r_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> are i.i.d. with mean <math id="A2.SS2.p17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A2.SS2.p17.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}(\pi_{\texttt{base}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}(\pi_{\texttt{base}})</annotation></semantics></math>,
we have <math id="A2.SS2.p17.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\Delta_{i}]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\Delta_{i}]=0</annotation></semantics></math> and, for <math id="A2.SS2.p17.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\neq j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\neq j</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\langle\Delta_{i},\Delta_{j}\rangle=\langle\mathbb{E}\Delta_{i},\mathbb{E}\Delta_{j}\rangle=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\langle\Delta_{i},\Delta_{j}\rangle=\langle\mathbb{E}\Delta_{i},\mathbb{E}\Delta_{j}\rangle=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p17.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p17.2.1" class="ltx_text">Thus only the diagonal terms survive in
equation <a href="#A2.E44" title="In Proof. ‣ B.2 Proof of Theoretical results in Section ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Results and Proofs ‣ Theoretical Limits of Language Model Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.44</span></a>:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\big\|R_{n}-r^{*}\big\|_{L^{2}(\pi_{\texttt{base}})}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\big\|R_{n}-r^{*}\big\|_{L^{2}(\pi_{\texttt{base}})}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n^{2}}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}\|\Delta_{i}\|_{L^{2}(\pi_{\texttt{base}})}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n^{2}}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}\|\Delta_{i}\|_{L^{2}(\pi_{\texttt{base}})}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n^{2}}\cdot n\,\mathbb{E}\|\Delta_{1}\|_{L^{2}(\pi_{\texttt{base}})}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n^{2}}\cdot n\,\mathbb{E}\|\Delta_{1}\|_{L^{2}(\pi_{\texttt{base}})}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}\,\mathbb{E}\|r_{1}-r^{*}\|_{L^{2}(\pi_{\texttt{base}})}^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}\,\mathbb{E}\|r_{1}-r^{*}\|_{L^{2}(\pi_{\texttt{base}})}^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.45)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p17.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p17.3.1" class="ltx_text">Set</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{2}\;\triangleq\;\mathbb{E}\|r_{1}-r^{*}\|_{L^{2}(\pi_{\texttt{base}})}^{2}&lt;\infty," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≜</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2}\;\triangleq\;\mathbb{E}\|r_{1}-r^{*}\|_{L^{2}(\pi_{\texttt{base}})}^{2}&lt;\infty,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p17.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p17.4.1" class="ltx_text">which is finite because each <math id="A2.SS2.p17.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded.
Then</span></p>
<table id="A2.E46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\big\|R_{n}-r^{*}\big\|_{L^{2}(\pi_{\texttt{base}})}^{2}=\frac{\sigma^{2}}{n}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\big\|R_{n}-r^{*}\big\|_{L^{2}(\pi_{\texttt{base}})}^{2}=\frac{\sigma^{2}}{n}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.46)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p18" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p18.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p18.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Cauchy–Schwarz,</span></p>
<table id="A2.E47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\big\|R_{n}-r^{*}\big\|_{L^{2}(\pi_{\texttt{base}})}\;\leq\;\Big(\mathbb{E}\big\|R_{n}-r^{*}\big\|_{L^{2}(\pi_{\texttt{base}})}^{2}\Big)^{1/2}\;\leq\;\frac{\sigma}{\sqrt{n}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mfrac><mi>σ</mi><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\big\|R_{n}-r^{*}\big\|_{L^{2}(\pi_{\texttt{base}})}\;\leq\;\Big(\mathbb{E}\big\|R_{n}-r^{*}\big\|_{L^{2}(\pi_{\texttt{base}})}^{2}\Big)^{1/2}\;\leq\;\frac{\sigma}{\sqrt{n}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.47)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p19" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p19.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p19.1.1" class="ltx_text">Taking expectations in equation <a href="#A2.E43" title="In Proof. ‣ B.2 Proof of Theoretical results in Section ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Results and Proofs ‣ Theoretical Limits of Language Model Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.43</span></a> and using
equation <a href="#A2.E47" title="In Proof. ‣ B.2 Proof of Theoretical results in Section ‣ Appendix B Theoretical Results and Proofs ‣ Theoretical Limits of Language Model Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.47</span></a> gives</span></p>
<table id="A2.E48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\big|\Delta(R_{n})-\Delta(r^{*})\big|\;\leq\;C\times\texttt{Var}(r^{*})^{1/2}\mathbb{E}\big\|R_{n}-r^{*}\big\|_{L^{2}(\pi_{\texttt{base}})}\;\leq\;\frac{C\texttt{Var}(r^{*})^{1/2}\sigma}{\sqrt{n}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Var</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\big|\Delta(R_{n})-\Delta(r^{*})\big|\;\leq\;C\times\texttt{Var}(r^{*})^{1/2}\mathbb{E}\big\|R_{n}-r^{*}\big\|_{L^{2}(\pi_{\texttt{base}})}\;\leq\;\frac{C\texttt{Var}(r^{*})^{1/2}\sigma}{\sqrt{n}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.48)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p19.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p19.2.1" class="ltx_text">In other words,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\big|\mathbb{E}_{\pi(R_{n},\lambda)}[r^{*}]-\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{r^{*},\lambda}}[r^{*}]\big|=O\!\left(\frac{\texttt{Var}(r^{*})^{1/2}}{\sqrt{n}}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.621em;" width="0.621em"><mi>O</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Var</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\big|\mathbb{E}_{\pi(R_{n},\lambda)}[r^{*}]-\mathbb{E}_{\pi_{r^{*},\lambda}}[r^{*}]\big|=O\!\left(\frac{\texttt{Var}(r^{*})^{1/2}}{\sqrt{n}}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p19.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p19.3.1" class="ltx_text">which yields the claimed <math id="A2.SS2.p19.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="O(n^{-1/2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(n^{-1/2})</annotation></semantics></math> rate.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>On the need for a new paradigm for reward modeling</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Proxy reward models are predominantly trained using the Bradley-Terry model, which frames human feedback strictly as binary pairwise comparisons over relative rankings, and thus fails to impose restrictions on preference residuals. Specifically, under the BT framework, the probability that a response <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{y}_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{y}_{w}</annotation></semantics></math> is preferred over a response <math id="A3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{y}_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{y}_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> given a prompt <math id="A3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math> is modeled as <math id="A3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pr(\mathbf{y}_{w}\succ\mathbf{y}_{l}\mid\mathbf{x})=\sigma(\tilde{r}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}_{w})-\tilde{r}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}_{l}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>≻</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr(\mathbf{y}_{w}\succ\mathbf{y}_{l}\mid\mathbf{x})=\sigma(\tilde{r}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}_{w})-\tilde{r}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}_{l}))</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> is the logistic function.
However, because this objective captures only the relative ordering of preferences, it provides no structural guarantee that the learned proxy reward <math id="A3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{r}</annotation></semantics></math> is quantitatively close to the unobserved gold reward <math id="A3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> in terms of preference residual.
Hence, a reward can perfectly minimize the BT loss with an arbitrarily large preference residual <math id="A3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The result in <a href="#Thmproposition3" title="Proposition 3 (The Impact of Proxy Rewards). ‣ 4.1 The Impact of Proxy Rewards in Reward Hacking ‣ 4 Proxy Rewards and a Justification for Reward Ensembling ‣ Theoretical Limits of Language Model Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Prop.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> shows that preference residual —uncontrolled in the BT framework— causes an exponential decrease in the gold reward, leading to reward hacking.
Conversely, <a href="#S4.E2" title="In Proposition 4 (A Deterministic Lipschitz Bound). ‣ 4.2 Why Reward Ensembling Mitigates Reward Hacking ‣ 4 Proxy Rewards and a Justification for Reward Ensembling ‣ Theoretical Limits of Language Model Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a> provides justification that if the preference residual is small, then reward hacking is mitigated, i.e., gains in performance are transferred to the evaluation using the gold reward.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Together, these results highlight <em id="A3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">the necessity for a new reward modeling paradigm</em>: we <span id="A3.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">must</span> incorporate preference magnitude to directly anchor the proxy reward, allowing us to actively measure and minimize its absolute <math id="A3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> distance to the gold reward.
Incorporating the magnitude of a preference would anchor the scale of the proxy, providing a direct mechanism to measure and minimize the preference residual.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Example: BT-invariant but increases the proxy–gold gap.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For a prompt <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math> suppose that the set of candidate responses decomposes into two disjoint clusters</p>
<table id="A3.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}=\mathcal{V}_{A}(\mathbf{x})\cup\mathcal{V}_{B}(\mathbf{x}),\qquad\mathcal{V}_{A}(\mathbf{x})\cap\mathcal{V}_{B}(\mathbf{x})=\varnothing," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}=\mathcal{V}_{A}(\mathbf{x})\cup\mathcal{V}_{B}(\mathbf{x}),\qquad\mathcal{V}_{A}(\mathbf{x})\cap\mathcal{V}_{B}(\mathbf{x})=\varnothing,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math> is the set of all possible responses. Also, consider that BT preference dataset for <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}</annotation></semantics></math> contains only within-cluster comparisons, i.e., every labeled pair <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbf{y}^{w},\mathbf{y}^{l})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>w</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbf{y}^{w},\mathbf{y}^{l})</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies either <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{y}^{w},\mathbf{y}^{l}\in\mathcal{V}_{A}(\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>w</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{y}^{w},\mathbf{y}^{l}\in\mathcal{V}_{A}(\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{y}^{w},\mathbf{y}^{l}\in\mathcal{V}_{B}(\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>w</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{y}^{w},\mathbf{y}^{l}\in\mathcal{V}_{B}(\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">When do clustered preference clusters arise?</h4>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This two-component structure naturally emerges in practice from mixture-of-sources candidate generation paired with within-source preference labeling. The following are examples of when this emerges:</p>
<ol id="A3.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Helpfulness and Harmlessness</span> We can generate one batch of candidates using a “helpful” decoding regime (cluster <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{A}(\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{A}(\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math>) and a second batch using a “safe/refusal” regime (cluster <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}_{B}(\mathbf{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}_{B}(\mathbf{x})</annotation></semantics></math>), as in HH-RLHF <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite>, where it is useful to train a <em id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">helpful</em> and <em id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">harmless</em> reward.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Subtle Safety Risks</span> To reduce annotation costs, alignment pipelines may use a <em id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">selective mechanism</em> where an AI labels simpler candidate pairs while humans evaluate only the most challenging ones. This inadvertently creates isolated data clusters.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Reasoning</span> A model might generate one batch of candidates using Chain-of-Thought reasoning, and another batch using direct answers. If human raters compare only CoT responses to other CoT responses (to judge the logic) and direct answers to direct answers (to judge conciseness), we have two clusters.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Tool Use</span> When training an LLM to use external tools (like web search), we may evaluate tool-use trajectories against other tool-uses to improve tool usage. These are never compared against a model simply answering from its own internal weights.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In these scenarios, the BT model learns accurate within-cluster rankings but leaves the relative reward offset between the clusters weakly identified.
The shift preserves all observed BT pairwise differences while potentially inflating the absolute preference residual <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">The theoretical Argument.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For any <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, define a modified proxy reward
<math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tilde{r}^{(M)}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\triangleq r^{*}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})+M\,\mathbf{1}\{\mathbf{y}\in\mathcal{V}_{A}(\mathbf{x})\}-M\,\mathbf{1}\{\mathbf{y}\in\mathcal{V}_{B}(\mathbf{x})\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≜</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>M</mi><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold"> 1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold"> 1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{r}^{(M)}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\triangleq r^{*}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})+M\,\mathbf{1}\{\mathbf{y}\in\mathcal{V}_{A}(\mathbf{x})\}-M\,\mathbf{1}\{\mathbf{y}\in\mathcal{V}_{B}(\mathbf{x})\}.</annotation></semantics></math>
For any observed preference pair <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathbf{y}^{w},\mathbf{y}^{l})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>w</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐲</mi><mi>l</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathbf{y}^{w},\mathbf{y}^{l})</annotation></semantics></math>, the pair lies within a single cluster; hence the <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>±</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm M</annotation></semantics></math> offsets cancel. Therefore every BT likelihood term is unchanged, and consequently <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{BT}}(\tilde{r}^{(M)})=\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{BT}}(r^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>BT</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>BT</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{BT}}(\tilde{r}^{(M)})=\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{BT}}(r^{*})</annotation></semantics></math>, which is the “optimal”.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">However, note that the preference residual can be written as</p>
<table id="A3.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\triangleq\tilde{r}^{(M)}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})-r^{*}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})=M\,\mathbf{1}\{\mathbf{y}\in\mathcal{V}_{A}(\mathbf{x})\}-M\,\mathbf{1}\{\mathbf{y}\in\mathcal{V}_{B}(\mathbf{x})\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≜</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>M</mi><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold"> 1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold"> 1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})\triangleq\tilde{r}^{(M)}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})-r^{*}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})=M\,\mathbf{1}\{\mathbf{y}\in\mathcal{V}_{A}(\mathbf{x})\}-M\,\mathbf{1}\{\mathbf{y}\in\mathcal{V}_{B}(\mathbf{x})\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Hence <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathcal{N}^{(M)}\|_{L^{2}(\pi_{\texttt{base}})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">base</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathcal{N}^{(M)}\|_{L^{2}(\pi_{\texttt{base}})}</annotation></semantics></math> (and <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{\mathbf{y}}|\mathcal{N}^{(M)}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>sup</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{\mathbf{y}}|\mathcal{N}^{(M)}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})|</annotation></semantics></math>) can be made arbitrarily large by increasing <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>, while the BT training objective remains identical.
At the same time, Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition3" title="Proposition 3 (The Impact of Proxy Rewards). ‣ 4.1 The Impact of Proxy Rewards in Reward Hacking ‣ 4 Proxy Rewards and a Justification for Reward Ensembling ‣ Theoretical Limits of Language Model Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> shows that the proxy-gold degradation is governed by the exponential tilt given as</p>
<table id="A3.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{e^{\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})/\lambda}}{\mathbb{E}_{\pi^{*}}\big[e^{\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})/\lambda}\big]}=\frac{e^{M/\lambda}\,\mathbf{1}\{\mathbf{y}\in\mathcal{V}_{A}(\mathbf{x})\}+e^{-M/\lambda}\,\mathbf{1}\{\mathbf{y}\in\mathcal{V}_{B}(\mathbf{x})\}}{\pi^{*}(\mathcal{V}_{A}(\mathbf{x}))e^{M/\lambda}+\pi^{*}(\mathcal{V}_{B}(\mathbf{x}))e^{-M/\lambda}}&gt;0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold"> 1</mn><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold"> 1</mn><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>π</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{e^{\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})/\lambda}}{\mathbb{E}_{\pi^{*}}\big[e^{\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y})/\lambda}\big]}=\frac{e^{M/\lambda}\,\mathbf{1}\{\mathbf{y}\in\mathcal{V}_{A}(\mathbf{x})\}+e^{-M/\lambda}\,\mathbf{1}\{\mathbf{y}\in\mathcal{V}_{B}(\mathbf{x})\}}{\pi^{*}(\mathcal{V}_{A}(\mathbf{x}))e^{M/\lambda}+\pi^{*}(\mathcal{V}_{B}(\mathbf{x}))e^{-M/\lambda}}&gt;0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(C.3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.3" class="ltx_p">which amplifies the mismatch between the proxy-aligned model <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(\tilde{r}^{(M)},\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(\tilde{r}^{(M)},\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> and the gold-aligned model <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{r^{*},\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{r^{*},\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math>, thereby increasing the gap <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> in Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition3" title="Proposition 3 (The Impact of Proxy Rewards). ‣ 4.1 The Impact of Proxy Rewards in Reward Hacking ‣ 4 Proxy Rewards and a Justification for Reward Ensembling ‣ Theoretical Limits of Language Model Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Reward-KL Pareto Frontier</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#A4.F4" title="In Appendix D Reward-KL Pareto Frontier ‣ Theoretical Limits of Language Model Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> validates the practicality of our proposed estimators for the Pareto frontier by showing the convergence of the entire theoretical Reward-KL Pareto frontier as a function of the number of base model samples <math id="A4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>.
Figure <a href="#A4.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ Appendix D Reward-KL Pareto Frontier ‣ Theoretical Limits of Language Model Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> illustrates the estimated frontiers using <math id="A4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in\{10,100,1000,10000\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>10,100</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1000</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10000</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in\{10,100,1000,10000\}</annotation></semantics></math> across both tasks (safety and summarization).
We observe that while small sample sizes (e.g., <math id="A4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=10</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>100</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">100</annotation></semantics></math>) systematically underestimate the achievable reward and prematurely truncate in the high-KL regime, the frontier rapidly stabilizes as <math id="A4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> increases.
This behavior directly reflects the mechanics of the estimators in <a href="#Thmdefinition1" title="Definition 1 (Monte Carlo Estimator for Δ(𝑟,𝑟^′)). ‣ 3.2 Estimating the Limits of Alignment from Data ‣ 3 Fundamental Limits of LLM Alignment. ‣ Theoretical Limits of Language Model Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Def.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and <a href="#Thmdefinition2" title="Definition 2 (Monte Carlo Estimator for KL Divergences). ‣ 3.2 Estimating the Limits of Alignment from Data ‣ 3 Fundamental Limits of LLM Alignment. ‣ Theoretical Limits of Language Model Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Def.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>: in the high-KL regime (which corresponds to a small penalty <math id="A4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>), the exponential tilt <math id="A4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{r/\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{r/\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> amplifies the variance of high-reward samples, thereby requiring a larger number of samples to achieve a tight estimate.
Crucially, the curves for <math id="A4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=1000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1000</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=1000</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=10000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10000</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=10000</annotation></semantics></math> are nearly overlapping across most of the KL spectrum.
This macro view of the frontier’s convergence complements the pointwise convergence guarantees of <a href="#Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 1 (Convergence of Estimator). ‣ 3.2 Estimating the Limits of Alignment from Data ‣ 3 Fundamental Limits of LLM Alignment. ‣ Theoretical Limits of Language Model Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Prop.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and <a href="#Thmproposition2" title="Proposition 2 (Convergence of KL Estimators). ‣ 3.2 Estimating the Limits of Alignment from Data ‣ 3 Fundamental Limits of LLM Alignment. ‣ Theoretical Limits of Language Model Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Prop.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, as well as the fixed-<math id="A4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> empirical results in <a href="#S4.F2" title="In 4.1 The Impact of Proxy Rewards in Reward Hacking ‣ 4 Proxy Rewards and a Justification for Reward Ensembling ‣ Theoretical Limits of Language Model Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and <a href="#S5.F3" title="In Dataset &amp; Tasks. ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Theoretical Limits of Language Model Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.
Ultimately, <a href="#A4.F4" title="In Appendix D Reward-KL Pareto Frontier ‣ Theoretical Limits of Language Model Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> confirms that a few thousand samples (around one thousand) are sufficient to reliably delineate the fundamental limits of alignment from base model samples alone.</p>
</div>
