<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A5.T2.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 2</span>: </span><span id="A5.T2.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">The hyper parameters swept for training Zephyr-7B-SFT-full on the BeaverTails dataset with <span id="A5.T2.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">GRPO</span> and <span id="A5.T2.7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">PPO</span>. The maximum reward gain is reported within the KL range that the theoretical limits are calculated for [0, 9.14]. The hyper-parameter run that is used in Figure <a href="#S1.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Theoretical Limits of Language Model Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> is <span id="A5.T2.7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">bolded</span>. For comparison, the maximum reward gain for the theoretical limit and BoN are 2.764 and 2.722, respectively.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
