<td id="A5.T3.st2.3.16.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">1e-5</td>
<td id="A5.T3.st2.3.16.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">64</td>
<td id="A5.T3.st2.3.16.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">0.7</td>
<td id="A5.T3.st2.3.16.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_r">4</td>
<td id="A5.T3.st2.3.16.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">0.143</td></tr>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A5.T3.st2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(b)</span> </span><span id="A5.T3.st2.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">PPO</span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A5.T3.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 3</span>: </span><span id="A5.T3.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">The hyper parameters swept for training Pythia 1B SFT on the TL;DR dataset with <span id="A5.T3.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">GRPO</span> and <span id="A5.T3.7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">PPO</span>. The maximum reward gain is reported within the KL range that the theoretical limits are calculated for [0, 7.96]. The hyper-parameter run that is used in Figure <a href="#S1.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Theoretical Limits of Language Model Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> is <span id="A5.T3.7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">bolded</span>. For comparison, the maximum reward gain for the theoretical limit and BoN are 0.387 and 0.385, respectively. For PPO, the two highest estimated reward gain runs were not used in the main body due to how noisy they are. (See Fig. <a href="#A5.F8" title="Figure 8 ‣ Appendix E Experimental Runs Hyper-parameter Sweeps ‣ Theoretical Limits of Language Model Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> for more details)</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A5.F5" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2605.07105v1/estimation_limit/beavertails_grpo_sweep-56.png" id="A5.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/213;" width="476" height="213" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A5.F5.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 5</span>: </span><span id="A5.F5.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Hyperparameter sweep for the fine-tuning Zephyr 7B SFT Full using GRPO on the Beavertails dataset. <span id="A5.F5.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">The plot shows the reward gain as the trained deviates from the base model. Abnormalities in the plotted lines are caused by training runs either plateauing before a KL of 9.14 or from oscillating between a small range of KL values.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A5.F6" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2605.07105v1/estimation_limit/beavertails_ppo_sweep_final.png" id="A5.F6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/181;" width="476" height="181" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A5.F6.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 6</span>: </span><span id="A5.F6.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Hyperparameter sweep for the fine-tuning Zephyr 7B SFT Full using PPO on the Beavertails dataset. <span id="A5.F6.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">The plot shows the reward gain as the trained deviates from the base model. Abnormalities in the plotted lines are caused by training runs either plateauing before a KL of 9.14 or from oscillating between a small range of KL values.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A5.F7" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2605.07105v1/estimation_limit/tldr_sweep_grpo-56.png" id="A5.F7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/209;" width="476" height="209" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A5.F7.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 7</span>: </span><span id="A5.F7.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Hyperparameter sweep for the fine-tuning Pythia 1B SFT using GRPO on the TLDR dataset.<span id="A5.F7.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> The plot shows the reward gain as the trained deviates from the base model. Abnormalities in the plotted lines are caused by training runs either plateauing before a KL of 7.96 or from oscillating between a small range of KL values.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A5.F8" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2605.07105v1/estimation_limit/ppo_tldr_sweep_55.png" id="A5.F8.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/175;" width="476" height="175" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A5.F8.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 8</span>: </span><span id="A5.F8.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Hyperparameter sweep for the fine-tuning Pythia 1B SFT using PPO on the TLDR dataset. <span id="A5.F8.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">The plot shows the reward gain as the trained deviates from the base model. Abnormalities in the plotted lines are caused by training runs either plateauing before a KL of 7.96 or from oscillating between a small range of KL values.</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Licenses of Used Assets</h2>

<div id="A6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The existing assets used in this paper are listed in Table <a href="#A6.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ Appendix F Licenses of Used Assets ‣ Theoretical Limits of Language Model Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.
The assets include publicly available datasets, model checkpoints, and software libraries used for the theoretical validation and empirical evaluation.
We cite the original creators of each asset and report the corresponding licenses.</p>
